# Barra Axial — Verificacion 1 Grado de Libertad
> Barra de 6 m empotrada, 3 elementos frame, fuerza axial F=100 kN
> u analitico = FL/(EA) = 100×6/(200e6×0.01) = 0.0003 m

---
## Datos

@{cells} |E = 200000000|A = 0.01|L = 6|F = 100|nElem = 3|

> Longitud por elemento:

dL = L / nElem

> Rigidez axial por elemento:

k_axial = E * A / dL

---
## Solucion Analitica

> Desplazamiento extremo libre:

u_analitico = F * L / (E * A)

---
## Modelo FEM (awatif)

> 4 nodos en X, 3 elementos, empotramiento en nodo 0, F axial en nodo 3

@{awatif}
nodes = [[0,0,0],[2,0,0],[4,0,0],[6,0,0]]
elements = [[0,1],[1,2],[2,3]]
supports = {0: [true,true,true,true,true,true]}
loads = {3: [100,0,0,0,0,0]}
E_val = 200000000
A_val = 0.01
Iz_val = 0.00001
Iy_val = 0.00001
G_val = 80000000
J_val = 0.00002
elasticities = {0: E_val, 1: E_val, 2: E_val}
areas = {0: A_val, 1: A_val, 2: A_val}
momentsOfInertiaZ = {0: Iz_val, 1: Iz_val, 2: Iz_val}
momentsOfInertiaY = {0: Iy_val, 1: Iy_val, 2: Iy_val}
shearModuli = {0: G_val, 1: G_val, 2: G_val}
torsionalConstants = {0: J_val, 1: J_val, 2: J_val}
show deformed scale:5000 nodeResults:deformations
@{end awatif}

---
## Comparacion

> El desplazamiento u_x del nodo 3 debe ser exactamente **0.0003 m** = 3e-4 m
> Error esperado: 0% (solucion exacta con elementos lineales bajo carga axial pura)
